        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Not every introduction follows that plan exactly. Preludes are relatively uncommon. In special circumstances, writers omit or rearrange other parts as well. Here are four common variations:",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                117,
                782,
                193
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
            "global_group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    193.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    193.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- When readers know a subject well, writers sometimes skip the shared context and open with the problem.",
            "block_bbox": [
                128,
                207,
                782,
                257
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 3,
            "global_group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    128.0,
                    207.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    207.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    257.0
                ],
                [
                    128.0,
                    257.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- When readers know a problem well, writers sometimes state the cost before the condition.",
            "block_bbox": [
                125,
                265,
                782,
                313
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    125.0,
                    265.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    265.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    313.0
                ],
                [
                    125.0,
                    313.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- When readers can be counted on to recognize the costs, writers sometimes skip them and just state the condition.",
            "block_bbox": [
                126,
                323,
                782,
                373
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    126.0,
                    323.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    323.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    373.0
                ],
                [
                    126.0,
                    373.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- When readers are willing to wait (which is rare), writers sometimes save their solution/main point/claim for the conclusion, ending the introduction with a promise that a solution will come.",
            "block_bbox": [
                129,
                381,
                783,
                458
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    129.0,
                    381.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    381.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    458.0
                ],
                [
                    129.0,
                    458.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Although many successful introductions use these variations, your best option is to follow the general pattern until you have lots of experience with it.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                471,
                782,
                522
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
